        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Curvature measures how much a Riemannian manifold deviates from being flat. The Riemann curvature tensor is the fundamental invariant; all other curvature quantities are derived from it."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-CURVATURE.md#003",
      "path": [
        "06-CURVATURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:differential-geometry:06-curvature, git-history:differential-geometry:06-curvature]",
        "canonical_path": "differential-geometry/06-CURVATURE.md",
        "concepts": "[curvature]",
        "current_path": "differential-geometry/06-CURVATURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:differential-geometry:curvature",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "differential-geometry",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[curvature]",
        "section": "differential-geometry",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Curvature",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                     CURVATURE HIERARCHY                          |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|  RIEMANN CURVATURE TENSOR R (most information)                  |\n|  R^l_{kij}: antisymmetric in i,j; Bianchi symmetries           |\n|  In n dimensions: n^2(n^2-1)/12 independent components         |\n|  n=2: 1 component = Gaussian curvature                          |\n|  n=4: 20 independent components (spacetime!)                    |\n|         |                                                         |\n|         v                                                         |\n|  RICCI TENSOR Ric                                               |\n|  Ric_{ij} = R^k_{ikj} (trace of Riemann over one index pair)   |\n|  Symmetric (0,2) tensor; n(n+1)/2 components                   |\n|         |                                                         |\n|         v                                                         |\n|  SCALAR CURVATURE R                                             |\n|  R = g^{ij} Ric_{ij} (trace of Ricci)                          |\n|  Single function on M                                           |\n|         |                                                         |\n|  SECTIONAL CURVATURE K(sigma)                                   |\n|  One number per 2-plane sigma in T_p M                          |\n|  Determines Riemann tensor if all sectional curvatures known    |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
